   Srinakharinwirot University},
ORCID-Numbers = {Friswold, Brooke/0000-0002-6484-5630
   Van de Water, Antoinette/0000-0001-9410-5417},
Funding-Acknowledgement = {King Mongkut's University of Technology Thonburi},
Funding-Text = {We extend our sincere gratitude to the Thai government and the
   Department of National Parks, Wildlife and Plant Conservation (DNP) and
   to the National Research Council of Thailand (NRCT) for granting
   permission to conduct this research. We are especially thankful to the
   Chiefs and staff of Kuiburi National Park, including the dedicated
   rangers and personnel at the Payang and Huay Luek ranger stations, for
   their collaboration, logistical assistance, and field support throughout
   the study. We gratefully acknowledge the Kui Buri Wildlife Ecotourism
   Club, including their leadership, drivers, and support staff for their
   cooperation and local knowledge. We acknowledge the support and
   exemplary assistance from the research assistants who were integral to
   the work, including Prapawin Phuttawanna (Miew), Kamolpawn Timtang
   (Mook), and Chidapha Oiumao (Bee). We immensely thank Bring The Elephant
   Home for their critical roles in research guidance, logistical support,
   and methodology insight, as well as conservation implementation and
   their support of community-engaged research in villages bordering KNP.
   We extend appreciation to the local community of Ruam Thai Village and
   the village head for their continued involvement and stewardship of
   elephant conservation initiatives. We also acknowledge King Mongkut's
   University of Technology Thonburi (KMUTT), the Conservation Ecology Lab,
   and the Institutional Animal Care and Use Committee (IACUC) at KMUTT for
   their institutional support and for approving the research protocol. We
   thank Dusit Ngoprasert for providing statistical analysis support. This
   study was made possible through support from the Petchra Pra Jom Klao
   Ph.D. Research Scholarship. Finally, we are grateful to the anonymous
   reviewers for their constructive feedback.},
